From 7047ef6d4bad0472409bf180ce004a436639a5c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AMLAudioTrim: aim the rate loop off to null the residual offset

Holding the rate takes the drift out but says nothing about where the flat line
sits: two cold starts of the same file settle tens of milliseconds apart and then
each holds its own offset perfectly, which is a rate loop doing exactly its job
and no more. Aim it off centre until the standing offset is gone, then let it
settle back.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

